available publications focus on the assemblage as a whole, detailed information 
on the precise dimensions and weight of the individual rings, including the one 
referred to here as the Ring of Nestor, is not consistently reported.[3][5] Some
descriptions mention a gold ring from the burial in general terms, while others 
emphasise the group of four gold signet rings without distinguishing their 
